<pdd-dependency>brain/library_index_Python.prompt</pdd-dependency>

% Goal

Maintain `brain/collection.py` as the shared GUI/CLI lifecycle for per-volume music collections while preserving its existing marker and portable-database APIs.

% Contract

R1 (MUST): A new collection reuses or creates `<data_dir>/collection.json` and `<data_dir>/library.sqlite3`; the default data directory is the nearest existing `clawdj/` at or above the chosen mount, otherwise `<mount>/clawdj/`.
R2 (MUST): Initialize a new SQLite with the normal library schema and persist validated scan roots only in that collection database.
R3 (MUST): Reusing an existing marker/database preserves all metadata, enrichment, dj_notes, bunches, roots and scan state.
R4 (MUST): The first explicit create/switch operation records a pre-existing local `brain/data/library.sqlite3` as a legacy collection without moving, deleting, merging or rewriting it.
R5 (MUST): GUI and CLI call the same lifecycle functions and produce the same registry/database state.
R6 (MUST): Estimate audio-file count without reading tags or calling any network/API service; scanning still requires explicit confirmation by the caller.
R7 (MUST NOT): Never run lyrics, chroma, Mixxx, network enrichment, playback, or a metadata scan merely by registering/activating a collection.
R8 (MUST NOT): Never overwrite a readable collection marker with a new identity or merge two collection databases during switching.
R9 (MUST): Keep absolute-path track identity unchanged.

% CLI

Support `python -m brain.collection list`, `status`, `new MOUNT [--root ROOT ...] [--name NAME] [--scan]`, and `use COLLECTION_ID`. `--scan` must use the same incremental scanner after showing the estimate; without `--scan`, creation only registers and activates.

% Output

- Primary output: `brain/collection.py`.

% Verification

- Run focused collection, CLI, marker, legacy and isolation tests; then full unittest and py_compile.
